{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Graphviz Network Topology Rendering.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Graphviz Network Topology Rendering.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"graphviz network topology rendering graphviz network topology rendering","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Graphviz Network Topology Rendering.md","fileName":"Graphviz Network Topology Rendering.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Graphviz Network Topology Rendering","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 18:30\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI-Assisted Network Automation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI-Assisted Network Automation","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Graphviz Network Topology Rendering.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Graphviz Network Topology Rendering.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"graphviz network topology rendering graphviz network topology rendering","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Graphviz Network Topology Rendering.md","fileName":"Graphviz Network Topology Rendering.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Graphviz Network Topology Rendering","heading":"Graphviz Network Topology Rendering","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Graphviz renders a topology from declarative node and edge definitions. In an AI-assisted workflow, the model produces DOT code, ordinary software saves it, and the Graphviz engine lays out the resulting graph. This keeps visual arrangement separate from the network relationships being described.\n\nRendering success proves only that the graph syntax is acceptable. An engineer should compare every device and connection with the original requirements and distinguish logical from physical relationships where necessary. Correcting the formal graph and rerendering is safer than manually editing a picture who